{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.SubgroupExtensionObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.SubgroupExtensionObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Subgroup.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Hom.Defs"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.not_extends_of_not_isPow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.not_extends_of_not_isPow","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SubgroupExtensionObstruction.lean#L82-L92","doc":"**The form the computation uses.**  If the obstruction is not an `n`-th power then no\nextension exists — so a non-trivial class in `A / Aⁿ` rules out every lift at once, with\nno hypothesis on the index `[M : L]`.\n\nApplied to `#7092`: `r (3e₀)` not being a cube in `K` forbids the diagonal `SL(3)` lift\noutright, rather than merely for the `e₀` that was computed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.pow_eq_of_extends","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.pow_eq_of_extends","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SubgroupExtensionObstruction.lean#L75-L80","doc":"**An extension forces the obstruction to be an `n`-th power.**  If `r` is the\nrestriction of a character `R` on all of `M`, then `r (e₀ ^ n) = (R e₀) ^ n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.liftObstruction_mul_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.liftObstruction_mul_mem","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SubgroupExtensionObstruction.lean#L57-L73","doc":"**The obstruction is well defined modulo `n`-th powers.**  Moving the witness `e₀`\nby an element of `L` multiplies it by an `n`-th power, so its class in `A / Aⁿ` — and in\nparticular whether that class is trivial — is independent of the choice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.liftObstruction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.liftObstruction","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/SubgroupExtensionObstruction.lean#L50-L55","doc":"The obstruction to extending `r : L →* A` across `e₀`, namely `r (e₀ ^ n)`.\n\nIts class in `A / Aⁿ` is the invariant; the bare value depends on `e₀`, and\n`liftObstruction_mul_mem` says exactly how. ","signatureChunk":0}]}